{
  "attributed_to": "Not the site tolerance. This campaign is the control for roundtrip_20_fdir1_attempt1_failed_audit.json: the only declared change is site_position_tolerance back from 0.07 to 0.030 m, and the campaign fails the same 11 of 20 while 8 of the 20 replicates change outcome. r6, r7, r8, r10, r11, r14 and r19 fail in both; r0, r1, r16 and r18 failed at 0.07 and complete at 0.030; r2, r3, r12 and r13 completed at 0.07 and fail at 0.030. An equal failure count with a different failing set makes the gate marginal rather than tolerance-dependent, which is what ruled the tolerance out and what withdrew the ADR 0008 raise. Attributed instead to core yaw injected by the transition itself and amplified by the drive that follows it, against a doorway with 0.02 m of slack per side.",
  "campaign_digest": "68529ca8572fbc7f11636b38ea5cb8c7629b7883f8040d22b2df32d38094b26c",
