  "diagnosis": "The yaw mechanism measured across the two failed attempts is recorded in docs/current_status.md, 'The 20-run round trip is not re-qualified': alignment ends within 0.030 rad of true in every run and is innocent, the transition adds +0.0105 to +0.1339 rad in every one of the 11 failures and -0.0571 to +0.0264 rad in the completions, and the drive to the doorway then adds same-signed drift in all 11 failures against mixed sign in the completions, reaching 0.1116-0.1548 rad at the doorway against at most 0.057 for 8 of 9 completions. Relocating pods drag the core, and ADR 0007 removed the accidental lateral grip world-fixed friction axes used to give a pod driving across its own axis; a 1.76 m skid-steer on 0.08 lateral friction is directionally unstable, and 0.88 m of half-length turns 0.1 rad into 0.09 m of nose excursion through a 0.70 m doorway. Real-time factor spans 0.516-0.971 over the 20 runs with all 20 realized disturbances unique, so neither host load nor a repeated disturbance draw explains the split. _trim_transition_yaw was written against this campaign and is still unverified: the 20-run gate has not been executed to completion since.",
  "disposition": "Retained as a FAILED qualification and not re-scored. Collected at a9554c8 with fdir1 (ADR 0007), margin_m 0.07, and site_position_tolerance back at 0.030 m after the ADR 0008 tolerance raise was withdrawn. 20 terminal records, 9 completed, 11 ended controller_failure after one transition. Raw records are results/qualification/roundtrip_20_fdir1_retry1_raw in the WSL clone (gitignored, about 117 MB). This summary was absent from the repository until 2026-09-30 and was recovered by re-running modular_robot_benchmarks.roundtrip_qualification audit against those surviving records: the output is byte-identical to the 2026-09-26 audit, whose stdout is retained beside them in roundtrip_20_fdir1_retry1_audit.log, and the audit code has not changed since. No outcome was re-scored in recovering it.",
